what a big day it was over at the talk  yes it was  shannon osborne is gone but her presence  was all over their first new show  since they suspended production  we haven't been together at the studio  since the week of march 10th  don't try and cry because if anyone  should be crying it should be me  during our break sharon decided to leave  the top  we need to process the events of that  day cheryl underwood opened the show  with an  intimate backstage message two weeks  after a cbs internal investigation  determined sharon's behavior quote  did not align with our values for a  respectful workplace  we'll be right back we have more topics  so don't go away i think we should stop  this  i didn't want to be perceived as the  angry black woman and and  that really scared me and it's difficult  to go back to that day  because i just feel the trauma i feel  fearful you know a little apprehensive  cheryl reunited with fellow co-hosts  elaine welteroth carriana nava and  amanda klutz on stage  underwood maintains she has not spoken  to sharon since the incident  i have not spoken to and do not have  any phone call missed or received but  there were  text messages sent to me and the reason  that i did not  respond to those text messages because  they were coming to me during the  internal investigation trauma therapist  dr anita phillips and diversity expert  dr donald e grant both were on hand to  help guide this difficult hour-long  conversation  about race and healing when you go back  and watch  what happened you will see two black  women  walking the same tightrope that  black women are walking every single day  in the workplace
 

